<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Maritime & Merchant Bank ASA (MMBANK) - Operational result for the first two months of 2019</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2019-03-18 17:01:28</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Maritime & Merchant Bank ASA (M&M) reports an unaudited operational result, after depreciation, before IFRS 9 and tax, for the first two months of 2019 of NOK 14.2 million (USD 1.67 million). The loan book, which in its entirety is secured by 1st priority mortgages in ocean going vessels, is NOK 2.18 billion (USD 256 million). There are no loan losses to be reported. Despite partly challenging shipping markets, M&M expects to continue to gradually increase its loan portfolio, domestically and in the international market.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Maritime & Merchant Bank ASA (MMBANK) - Notice of Annual Shareholders Meeting</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2019-02-14 16:53:37</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>The Board of Directors of Maritime & Merchant Bank ASA (the "Company") hereby summons the annual shareholders meeting in the Company.<br>Time: March 1st 2019, 12:00<br>Place: Maritime & Merchant Bank ASA, Haakon VII’s street 1, 3rd floor</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
<a href="/public/news/18286.pdf">
Maritime & Merchant Bank ASA - Notice of Annual Shareholders Meeting - 190214.pdf</a>
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Maritime & Merchant Bank ASA (MMBANK) - Financial Report 31-12-2018</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2019-02-14 16:47:53</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Maritime & Merchant Bank ASA (M&M) had an operating profit before tax of USD 1.250.045 in its second operational year.<br>Depreciation and loss allowance (IFRS 9) constitutes USD 2.672.008, thus M&M had a modified operating <br>result (free cashflow) of USD 3.922.829 in 2018. M&M has not experienced any losses in its operational history. <br> <br>The activity has generally been high during the year with an increasing inflow of loan applications from our domestic market <br>and from a growing specter of international customers resulting in a growth in the loan portfolio of disbursed loans from USD<br>92 mill by end 2017 to USD 249 mill as per 31.12. 2018. M&M is primarily serving the project oriented market and the time<br>that passes from signing the loan documentation until disbursement may vary quite significantly due to various <br>operational circumstances beyond our control. M&M would therefore hold a certain order reserve of committed (undisbursed) loans <br>at any time. All loans granted by M&M are secured by 1st priority mortgages and in addition a collateral package adapted to <br>the specific project we are financing. Our main focus is to finance standard vessels within the main segments dry bulk,<br>tankers (crude, product, chemical), container and gas.  <br> <br>We look optimistically into 2019 and for the further growth of our services. M&M will continue to work hard in order to become <br>the preferred bank for secured project financing in the shipping sector. Our objective is to be a professional partner for our customers<br>in their work for materializing new projects.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
<a href="/public/news/18285.pdf">
Maritime  & Merchant Bank ASA - Financial Report 31-12-2018 - 190214.pdf</a>
<br>
<a href="/public/news/18285_2.pdf">
Maritime & Merchant Bank ASA - Report on the Audit of the Financial Statements - 190214.pdf</a>
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Maritime & Merchant Bank ASA (MMBANK) - Shareholders Letter</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2018-12-19 12:40:59</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>In ‘’Shareholders Letter’’ sent out today to the shareholders of Maritime & Merchant Bank ASA, the Chairman Endre Røsjø highlights<br>a strong growth in the bank  with a loan portfolio increasing from USD 100 mill at the start of the year and to the current level which within short time will reach USD 300 mill. He also points out that the third quarter operating result (after depreciation; before tax) was approx. USD 1 mill as previously reported, and that the positive development has continued during 4th quarter. Furthermore, the Chairman comments that the expectation for next year is for a continued organic growth resulting in a profitable full calendar year 2019.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>MMBANK: Maritime & Merchant Bank ASA (M&M) is registered on the NOTC-list</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2018-11-20 08:03:26</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Maritime & Merchant Bank ASA (M&M) is registered on the NOTC-list as of 20 November 2018 with ticker code “MMBANK”. The Company has 7,252,333 common shares outstanding each with a par value NOK 10.00, all of which are registered in VPS with ISIN code NO0010700628. Based on the last share issue completed on 25 May 2018, the market capitalization of the Company is NOK 744,669,552 (NOK 102.68 per share). The Company has entered into an agreement with NOTC AS whereby it will be able to use the reporting system as of 20 November 2018.<br><br>Maritime & Merchant Bank ASA (M&M) is a specialized bank for the shipping and offshore sector offering term loans secured by 1st priority mortgages. The bearing principle for M&M is to combine deep industrial insight and experience with first class banking craftsmanship and by this serve our customers in an efficient and professional manner. Our target customers are small and medium sized shipowners, project arrangers and investors in the industry. We are serving customers from all the important shipping centers in the world from our office in Oslo city. We are offering different deposit products for NOK and USD. The strategy for M&M going forward is to continuously refine our scalable operational platform and our core competence, progressing the upbuilding of a diversified portfolio of secured loans and develop the bank further to a leading player within our target market.<br><br>Please see attached Financial Report Q3 2018</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
<a target="_blank" href="http://www.mmbank.no">
http://www.mmbank.no</a>
<a href="/public/news/18095.pdf">
Maritime  Merchant  Bank - Financial Report 30-09-2018.pdf</a>
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
</table>

